INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction to the Role of 75mm Pipe in Farm Economics</h2>\n<p>One of the primary challenges for producers in modern agriculture is managing infrastructure costs. In drip and tape irrigation systems, a main line with a diameter of 75 mm is typically used in small to medium-sized farms, or as a sub-main line in larger farms. A precise understanding <strong>of the cost of 75mm threaded pipe</strong> and its associated components can make a significant difference in final profitability. Many farmers only consider the price per meter of the pipe, ignoring secondary costs such as fittings, hardware, and installation labor. This article aims to provide a practical guide by explaining all cost factors to help with a realistic estimate. Initial costs may seem negligible, but over a five-to-ten-year period, selecting the right pipe material and fittings can reduce operational and maintenance costs by up to 30%. Therefore, a superficial look at retail price tags without considering amortization (functionality) costs does not reflect the true cost.</p>\n<p>The choice of pipe type (threaded or welded) and manufacturer brand directly impacts system durability and, ultimately, annual maintenance costs. Higher-quality pipes offer greater resistance to UV exposure and temperature fluctuations. Therefore, technical and economic details will be discussed in the following sections. To better understand the relationship between pipe type and efficiency, you can read the article on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%87-%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%b2%d8%a7%db%8c%d8%b4-%d8%b9%d9%85%d8%b1-%d9%85%d9%81%db%8c%d8%af-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be/">how to extend the useful life of tape lines</a> ; a healthy main line ensures the proper function of sub-lines and pressure stability throughout the season.</p>\n\n<h2>Factors affecting the final price of 75mm threaded pipe</h2>\n<h3>Material type and raw material quality</h3>\n<p>Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) pipes are available in various A and K grades. Pipes meeting higher standards cost more but offer greater resistance to pressure and environmental corrosive factors. In sandy farms or areas with acidic soil, selecting pipes with enhanced protection can reduce early replacement costs. Pipe wall thickness (SN) is also a critical parameter affecting the base cost. Choosing a pipe with a higher SN rating means a higher initial cost but a longer service life.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/هزینه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-در-مزرعه-برآورد-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="هزینه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر در مزرعه: برآورد - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product cost farm budget 75 millimeter threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>Pricing based on meter and carton</h3>\n<p>Manufacturers typically quote prices per carton (e.g., 4-meter or 6-meter lengths). When estimating costs, the cutting waste factor must also be considered. Normally, there is 5 to 10 percent waste associated with cutting and joints. Therefore, when budgeting, always add 10 percent to the calculated length for purchase. Additionally, transportation costs from the central warehouse to the farm can constitute a significant portion of the total purchase cost and should not be overlooked.</p>\n\n<h2>Financial estimation and reference tables</h2>\n<p>To achieve a structured overview, it is advisable to categorize the costs. Below is a conceptual table of cost components for a 5,000-square-meter farm. Note that prices are variable, and these tables are intended to illustrate the cost structure rather than reflect real-time market prices. The indicated percentage shares are based on recent market averages for piping materials.</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Material / Service</th>\n<th>Unit</th>\n<th>Technical Specifications</th>\n<th>Estimated Budget Share</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75 mm threaded pipe</td>\n<td>Meters</td>\n<td>Cuts and replacements</td>\n<td>40% to 50%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fittings and connections (No. 75)</td>\n<td>Individual</td>\n<td>Tee, elbow, tee</td>\n<td>15% to 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Control equipment (valves, filter)</td>\n<td>Set</td>\n<td>Ball valve, disc filter</td>\n<td>20% to 25%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Installation and commissioning labor</td>\n<td>hectare</td>\n<td>labor and machinery</td>\n<td>10%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>To finalize your budget, use the following formula. Calculate the total length of main and lateral lines and multiply by the cost per meter of pipe. Then, determine the number of fittings based on the connection pattern (loop, tree, or grid). Finally, add the cost of control equipment. This calculation is more accurate than verbal estimation. To understand the relationship between equipment and efficiency, studying the cost of a drip line per hectare can broaden your perspective on comparing system types.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/هزینه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-در-مزرعه-برآورد-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="هزینه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر در مزرعه: برآورد - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>product cost farm budget threaded pipe 75 millimeter</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for reducing threaded pipe costs</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Optimal network design:</strong> Using a simple tree pattern instead of a complex grid network in dry-climate farms can reduce pipe length. Each meter less of pipe means lower costs.</li>\n<li><strong>Reduction of cutting losses:</strong> Using moving cut fibers and smart pipe storage reduces waste. Standard pre-cuts of 20 or 40 meters are better than short cuts.</li>\n<li><strong>Proper use of connectors:</strong> Crane connectors (couplets) are cheaper than Number connectors, but for high durability at high-pressure points, buy Number connectors. Carefully combining the two optimizes cost.</li>\n<li><strong>Seasonal maintenance:</strong> Cleaning filters and checking valves at the end of the season prevents pipe failure in the following year due to sudden pressure spikes. This directly prevents pipe replacement costs.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>In addition to the above points, note the compatibility of pipes with drip tapes. If using specific tapes, ensure the operating pressure of control valves is compatible with 75mm pipes. You can learn more about system configuration costs by reviewing drip tape products. Considering the cost of purchasing field drip tape and reviewing available models is also very practical.</p>\n\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Does the price of 75 mm threaded pipe include fittings?</strong><br>No, pipe prices are typically listed per meter excluding fittings. Fittings must be calculated separately based on the design layout.</li>\n<li><strong>What are the best brands for 75 mm pipes?</strong><br>Select reputable Iranian brands that meet ISO standards. Low-cost brands with thin wall thickness lead to higher long-term costs.</li>\n<li><strong>What is the service life of a 75 mm pipe?</strong><br>Under standard conditions, the service life is 10 to 20 years. Improper use of water pressure reduces this lifespan.</li>\n<li><strong>How do we calculate the line pressure?</strong><br>Calculate based on the field elevation and the length of the main line. For sloped farms, you need a pressure regulator.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>Estimate <strong>Cost of 75 mm threaded pipe</strong> This is a process that does not end with simply calculating area. Factors such as waste coefficients, connection types, control equipment, and even soil type affect the total cost. Professional farmers usually allocate a budget with a 15–20 percent safety margin to account for unforeseen issues. Using up-to-date data and consulting installation experts is the key to successful investment in irrigation infrastructure. By combining technical knowledge with detailed financial analysis, you can prevent system failure during the initial years of use. For the next steps, it is recommended to review related articles on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%B9%D8%AF%D8%B3-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Seed rate per hectare</a> or other agricultural items on this website to gain a broader perspective on the entire production cycle.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/هزینه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-در-مزرعه-برآورد-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="هزینه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر در مزرعه: برآورد - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Product cost farm budget 75 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D8%B4%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D9%86%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%B7-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%AA%DA%A9%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA/">Purified drinking water in Tikrit</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%AC%D9%88-%D8%B4%D8%B4-%D9%BE%D8%B1-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Barley and wheat yield per hectare</a></p>\n<p></p>\n','75mm AFP Garden Hose Cost on Farms: Precise Budgeting Estimates','Are you looking for an accurate cost estimate for 75 mm threaded pipe for your farm? Learn the calculation formulas, escalation factors, and budget allocation methods in this article to avoid incorrect purchases.','publish','closed','closed','75mm-afp-hose-cost-farm-budgeting',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:prod-011:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
